"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D council tax (area bill)","value":2327.24,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D \u2014 council's own element","value":304.56,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"}]}},"dossier":{"summary":{"summary":"Basildon's gross external debt reached \u00a3695.4m at 31 March 2026 (net \u00a3674.4m after \u00a321.0m of investments), up \u00a336.1m over the year, though it stayed comfortably inside its \u00a3825m Authorised Limit and \u00a3775m Operational Boundary (peak in-year debt \u00a3707.4m). The council carries meaningful exposure to its housing subsidiary Sempra Homes Limited \u2014 \u00a355.0m of long-term loans, \u00a37.9m of short-term loans and \u00a324.5m of shares \u2014 and its legacy commercial property portfolio (Stevenage, Bath, Tunbridge Wells, Richmond, Northampton) is now worth \u00a330.1m against an acquisition cost of \u00a341.8m, with gross yield of 4.96% undershooting the 5% target. No Prudential Indicators were breached and no new PWLB borrowing was taken in the year; instead the council drew \u00a3171.0m of new short-term loans from other local authorities.","fy":"2025/26","as_of_doc":"Capital and Investment Strategy Annual Report 2025/26","as_of_url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info/documents/s158433/Enc. 1 for Capital and Investment Strategy Annual Report 202526 v2.pdf","as_of_date":"2026-07-15","signals":[{"code":"company-exposure","headline":"\u00a355.0m long-term loans + \u00a37.9m short-term loans + \u00a324.5m shares outstanding to subsidiary Sempra Homes Limited at 31 Mar 2026","why":"This is a large, concentrated exposure to a single council-owned company whose repayment capacity depends on the housing company's own performance."},{"code":"borrowing-increase","headline":"Net external debt rose \u00a336.1m in the year to \u00a3674.4m (gross \u00a3695.4m); the council took \u00a3171.0m of new short-term borrowing from other local authorities while repaying \u00a3150.0m","why":"Rising debt levels, especially short-term inter-authority borrowing, increase both debt-servicing costs and rollover/refinancing exposure."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"cfr","value":"\u00a3777.4m (average, whole council); HRA mid-year CFR \u00a3272.9m, HRA debt maintained at that level","as_at":"2025/26","page":4},{"name":"gross external debt","value":"\u00a3695.4m (Borrowing \u00a3495.5m + Finance leases \u00a3199.9m), up from \u00a3690.3m opening","as_at":"2026-03-31","page":2},{"name":"net external debt","value":"\u00a3674.4m, up \u00a336.1m over the year (net of \u00a321.0m treasury investments)","as_at":"2026-03-31","page":2},{"name":"borrowing indicators","value":"Peak external debt in year \u00a3707.4m vs Operational Boundary \u00a3775m and Authorised Limit \u00a3825m \u2014 neither breached","as_at":"2025/26","page":3},{"name":"la borrowing short term","value":"\u00a3171.0m drawn from other local authorities in year; \u00a3150.0m of other-LA borrowing repaid; no new PWLB borrowing taken","as_at":"2025/26","page":3},{"name":"financing costs to net revenue","value":"Average debt \u00a3691.562m, cumulative interest paid \u00a322.919m, average rate 3.31%","as_at":"2025/26","page":4},{"name":"treasury outturn vs budget","value":"Investment income outturn \u00a31.9m at 5.21% average rate on \u00a336.5m average principal, vs budget of \u00a30.5m at 3.30% on \u00a316.5m","as_at":"2025/26","page":4},{"name":"commercial portfolio","value":"Acquisition cost \u00a341.810m, current value \u00a330.135m across 5 sites (Stevenage, Bath, Tunbridge Wells, Richmond, Northampton); gross yield 4.96% vs 5% target, net yield 0.62%","as_at":"2026-03-31","page":6},{"name":"company lending","value":"Sempra Homes Limited: \u00a355.0m long-term loans + \u00a37.9m short-term loans (cash flow support) + \u00a324.5m shares (held via Basildon Borough Enterprises); rate not stated in this report","as_at":"2026-03-31","page":7}],"commercial":{"commercial_portfolio":{"value":"Acquisition cost \u00a341.810m, current value \u00a330.135m across 5 sites (Stevenage, Bath, Tunbridge Wells, Richmond, Northampton); gross yield 4.96% vs 5% target, net yield 0.62%","as_at":"2026-03-31","page":6,"doc":"Capital and Investment Strategy Annual Report 2025/26"},"company_lending":{"value":"Sempra Homes Limited: \u00a355.0m long-term loans + \u00a37.9m short-term loans (cash flow support) + \u00a324.5m shares (held via Basildon Borough Enterprises); rate not stated in this report","as_at":"2026-03-31","page":7,"doc":"Capital and Investment Strategy Annual Report 2025/26"}},"tms_components":null},"compliance":null,"documents":[],"read_documents":[{"title":"Capital and Investment Strategy Annual Report 2025/26","url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info/documents/s158433/Enc. 1 for Capital and Investment Strategy Annual Report 202526 v2.pdf","committee":"Audit and Risk Committee","date":"2026-07-15","category":"treasury","fy":"2025/26"}],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-10-01","committee":"Local Government Reorganisation (LGR) Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info"},{"date":"2026-10-08","committee":"Housing Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info"},{"date":"2026-10-13","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Commission","time":"7.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info"},{"date":"2026-10-15","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Council","time":"7.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info"},{"date":"2026-10-28","committee":"Regeneration Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info"},{"date":"2026-11-04","committee":"Audit and Risk Committee","time":"7.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info"},{"date":"2026-11-10","committee":"Finance, Procurement and Efficiency Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-23","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info"},{"date":"2026-09-02","committee":"Audit and Risk Committee","time":"7.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Finance, Procurement and Efficiency Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Council","time":"7.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Basildon Council forecasts \u00a33.4m budget overspend as emergency housing costs surge","lead":"Basildon Council's Cabinet heard on 24 September that it is forecast to overspend its general fund budget by \u00a33.4m, or 6.8 per cent, for the financial year. The council budgeted to spend \u00a349.3m but now expects to spend \u00a352.6m. More than three-fifths of the overspend comes from temporary accommodation, which is forecast to cost \u00a37.7m against a budget of \u00a35.6m\u2014a 37 per cent overspend. The council also expects to collect only \u00a348k in planning fees against a budgeted \u00a3860k. The papers show that an efficiency savings programme meant to deliver \u00a3766k is now forecast to cost \u00a320k instead, contributing to the overall shortfall.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Enc. 2 - Capital &amp; Investment Strategy Q1 Report","paper_url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info/documents/s159412/159412.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Basildon forecasts \u00a33.4m overspend on council services","lead":"Basildon Council has forecast an overspend of \u00a33.4m on its day-to-day running costs (revenue spending), about 6.8 per cent of the total budget. The largest factor is temporary accommodation for homeless people, forecast at \u00a37.7m against a budget of \u00a35.6m. Planning fees are forecast at \u00a348,000 against a budget of \u00a3860,000. The council's transformation programme, intended to deliver \u00a3766,000 in savings, is now forecast to cost \u00a320,000. The council will need to find further savings or use its reserves (money set aside) to balance its budget.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Enc. 2 - Capital &amp; Investment Strategy Q1 Report","paper_url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info/documents/s159412/159412.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Basildon faces \u00a33.4m budget overspend driven by housing costs","lead":"Basildon Council is forecasting an overspend of \u00a33.4m, or 6.8 per cent of its day-to-day spending budget. Papers to its Cabinet show the council expects to spend \u00a352.6m against a budget of \u00a349.3m. Temporary accommodation is the largest single driver, forecast to cost \u00a37.7m against a budget of \u00a35.6m\u2014an overspend of \u00a32.1m, or 37 per cent, representing more than three-fifths of the total overspend. The council is also facing a \u00a3812,000 shortfall in planning fee income, forecast at \u00a348,000 against a budgeted \u00a3860,000. The organisation transformation programme is meanwhile forecast to cost \u00a320,000 instead of delivering budgeted savings of \u00a3766,000.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Enc. 2 - Capital &amp; Investment Strategy Q1 Report","paper_url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info/documents/s159412/159412.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Enc. 1 - Budget Monitoring Detail by Portfolio","paper_url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info/documents/s159411/159411.pdf","headline":"Commercial property income is underperforming; Out of Borough commercial forecast \u00a3722k below budget","detail":"Out of Borough commercial property is forecast to deliver \u00a32.163m against a budget of \u00a32.885m, a shortfall of \u00a3722k (25% adverse). The council also shows shortfalls in Garages (\u00a3449k) and Strategic Assets (\u00a3227k), indicating broader underperformance in commercial property income.","category":"income","matters":"Shortfalls in commercial property income mean the council's income assumptions are not being met; this erodes the revenue available to fund services.","figures":"Out of Borough commercial: \u00a3722k shortfall (25%); Garages: \u00a3449k shortfall; Strategic Assets: \u00a3227k shortfall","quote":"Commercial (Out of Borough) (2,885) (2,163) 722 (25.0%)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Enc. 1 - Budget Monitoring Detail by Portfolio","paper_url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info/documents/s159411/159411.pdf","headline":"The Organisation Transformation Programme is forecast to cost \u00a320k instead of delivering budgeted savings of \u00a3766k","detail":"The OTP was budgeted to deliver \u00a3766k of cost savings (shown as negative cost). The latest forecast shows it costing \u00a320k, representing an adverse movement of \u00a3786k (102.6%). The planned savings are not materializing.","category":"savings","matters":"A transformation programme that fails to deliver planned savings means the council's efficiency strategy is not working; the \u00a3766k that was counted on to fund services is unavailable.","figures":"Budgeted saving \u00a3766k, forecast cost \u00a320k, adverse variance \u00a3786k (102.6%)","quote":"Organisation Transformation Programme (OTP) (766) 20 786 (102.6%)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Enc. 1 - Budget Monitoring Detail by Portfolio","paper_url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info/documents/s159411/159411.pdf","headline":"Planning fee income is forecast at \u00a348k against a \u00a3860k budget, a shortfall of \u00a3812k (94.5%)","detail":"Planning fee income is now forecast to deliver only \u00a348k compared to the budgeted \u00a3860k. This represents a shortfall of \u00a3812k or 94.5% of budgeted income.","category":"income","matters":"A 94.5% collapse in planning income means the council is not receiving expected discretionary revenue and requires alternative funding sources or service reductions.","figures":"Budget \u00a3860k, forecast \u00a348k, shortfall \u00a3812k (94.5%)","quote":"Planning 860 48 (812) (94.5%)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Enc. 1 - Budget Monitoring Detail by Portfolio","paper_url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info/documents/s159411/159411.pdf","headline":"Temporary accommodation costs are forecast at \u00a37.671m, \u00a32.082m above budget (37.3% overspend)","detail":"The largest single variance in the budget is temporary accommodation, which accounts for 62% of the total council overspend. Costs are forecast at \u00a37.671m against a budget of \u00a35.589m, a variance of \u00a32.082m or 37.3%.","category":"demand","matters":"Temporary accommodation is a demand-driven service; an overspend of this magnitude indicates demand significantly exceeds what was planned and requires either additional funding or service intervention.","figures":"Budgeted \u00a35.589m, forecast \u00a37.671m, overspend \u00a32.082m (37.3%)","quote":"Temporary Accommodation 5,589 7,671 2,082 37.3%","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Enc. 1 - Budget Monitoring Detail by Portfolio","paper_url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info/documents/s159411/159411.pdf","headline":"Basildon is forecasting a general fund overspend of \u00a33.363m (6.8% of total budget)","detail":"The council's budget monitoring shows budgeted spend of \u00a349.261m but a forecast spend of \u00a352.624m, creating an overspend of \u00a33.363m or 6.8% of the budget. This is a material variance indicating the council's financial plan is not on track.","category":"overspend","matters":"A material overspend indicates the council's financial plan is not being delivered and requires mitigation, whether through reserve draws, service reductions, or additional funding.","figures":"Budget \u00a349.261m, forecast \u00a352.624m, overspend \u00a33.363m (6.8%)","quote":"Grand Total 49,261 52,624 3,363 6.8%","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-24"},"name":"Basildon","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-25","since_iso":"2026-08-26","distress":false,"headline":"Commercial property income is underperforming; Out of Borough commercial forecast \u00a3722k below budget","lead":"Shortfalls in commercial property income mean the council's income assumptions are not being met; this erodes the revenue available to fund services.","also":["42 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Local Government Reorganisation (LGR) Scrutiny Committee on 2026-10-01","n_findings":43,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Enc. 1 - Budget Monitoring Detail by Portfolio","top_paper_url":"https://www.basildonmeetings.info/documents/s159411/159411.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":69,"news_drafts_total":3}}